==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|synchronous|alt1=synchron(ous)|-icity}}. From {{w|Jungian psychology}} in the 1920s. {{l|en|surface analysis#Noun|Surface analysis}}, {{affix|en|syn-|chrono-|alt2=chron-|-icity}}; historically, see {{m|en|synchronous#Etymology|synchronous § Etymology}}.

